{"absent":["Heap sift ordering predicate and callback layout beyond swap hook not shown","Non inline heap core bodies for peek full and sift operations not in fragments","Heap and plist locking and concurrency requirements not shown","Plist insertion deletion and priority order maintenance not in fragments","Radix preload allocation release and lock discipline not shown","Extended array chunk and mark numeric values not in fragments","Overflow builtin details and maximum size sentinel definition not in fragments","Checked plist accessor warning behavior beyond empty test not in fragments"],"dossier":"D14","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heapify_all_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heapify_all_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_pop_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_pop_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_del_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_del_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_init","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_peek","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_full","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_sift_down","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_sift_up","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heapify_all","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_pop","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_pop_push","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_push","include/linux/min_heap.h::min_heap_del"],"text":"Typed heap macros forward to a common byte oriented core with element size plus callbacks and opaque argument, covering bulk build, removal of smallest, replacement of smallest, insertion, indexed removal, initialization, peek, full test and sift helpers."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heapify_all_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_del_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_push_inline"],"text":"Occupancy count stays within capacity, storage is a flat element array, heap order is restored through sift up or down after each mutation, and bulk construction normalizes arbitrary initial contents."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_del_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_push_inline"],"text":"Pop, push and indexed delete report success as boolean and leave the heap ordered on success, while pop plus push unconditionally overwrites the smallest slot and then restores order without a capacity check."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_pop_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_push_inline","include/linux/min_heap.h::__min_heap_del_inline"],"text":"Popping or deleting when empty and pushing when full emit a once only warning and report failure instead of mutating state, and deleting the final slot short circuits without further reordering."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::min","include/linux/minmax.h::max","include/linux/minmax.h::umin","include/linux/minmax.h::umax","include/linux/minmax.h::min3","include/linux/minmax.h::max3","include/linux/minmax.h::min_t","include/linux/minmax.h::max_t","include/linux/minmax.h::__types_ok","include/linux/minmax.h::__types_ok3","include/linux/minmax.h::__cmp","include/linux/minmax.h::__cmp_once","include/linux/minmax.h::__cmp_once_unique","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_cmp","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_cmp_once","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_op3","include/linux/minmax.h::__cmp_op_min","include/linux/minmax.h::__cmp_op_max","include/linux/minmax.h::__sign_use","include/linux/minmax.h::__is_nonneg.alt_1","include/linux/minmax.h::__is_nonneg.alt_2","include/linux/minmax.h::__typecheck"],"text":"Comparison family offers careful two value and three value extrema, unsigned forcing extrema, and explicitly typed extrema, built on shared helpers that classify signedness, compare once saved operands, and select smaller or larger."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::__types_ok","include/linux/minmax.h::__types_ok3","include/linux/minmax.h::__sign_use","include/linux/minmax.h::__is_nonneg.alt_1","include/linux/minmax.h::__is_nonneg.alt_2","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_cmp_once","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_op3","include/linux/minmax.h::__cmp_once_unique","include/linux/minmax.h::min","include/linux/minmax.h::max","include/linux/minmax.h::umin","include/linux/minmax.h::umax","include/linux/minmax.h::min3","include/linux/minmax.h::max3"],"text":"Careful forms evaluate each input once into uniquely named temporaries, reject mixed signedness pairings at build time, treat unsigned coercion through unsigned arithmetic, and choose result by strict less or greater relation."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::min_not_zero","include/linux/minmax.h::__clamp","include/linux/minmax.h::__clamp_once","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_clamp","include/linux/minmax.h::clamp","include/linux/minmax.h::clamp_t","include/linux/minmax.h::clamp_val"],"text":"Bounding family limits a value between low and high with inferred, explicit or value derived typing, plus a zero aware minimum that ignores zero inputs unless both are zero."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::__clamp_once","include/linux/minmax.h::__careful_clamp","include/linux/minmax.h::clamp","include/linux/minmax.h::clamp_t","include/linux/minmax.h::clamp_val"],"text":"Clamp helpers evaluate inputs once, fail the build when low exceeds high under constant evaluation, enforce three way type compatibility, and otherwise return high when above range, low when below range, else the value."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::__minmax_array","include/linux/minmax.h::min_array","include/linux/minmax.h::max_array","include/linux/minmax.h::in_range64","include/linux/minmax.h::in_range32","include/linux/minmax.h::in_range","include/linux/minmax.h::swap","include/linux/minmax.h::MIN","include/linux/minmax.h::MAX","include/linux/minmax.h::MIN_T","include/linux/minmax.h::MAX_T"],"text":"Array helpers fold an extrema operation from the last element toward the first, range helpers test membership with width selected from operand sizes, swap exchanges same type lvalues in place, and raw uppercase forms compare without safety checks."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::in_range64","include/linux/minmax.h::in_range32","include/linux/minmax.h::in_range"],"text":"Fixed width range tests use unsigned wraparound subtraction of start from the candidate and report membership when the distance is below length, with a generic selector choosing thirty two or sixty four bit form."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/overflow.h::__must_check_overflow","include/linux/overflow.h::check_add_overflow","include/linux/overflow.h::check_sub_overflow","include/linux/overflow.h::check_mul_overflow","include/linux/overflow.h::check_shl_overflow","include/linux/overflow.h::wrapping_add","include/linux/overflow.h::wrapping_sub","include/linux/overflow.h::wrapping_mul","include/linux/overflow.h::wrapping_assign_add","include/linux/overflow.h::wrapping_assign_sub","include/linux/overflow.h::__type_half_max","include/linux/overflow.h::__type_max","include/linux/overflow.h::type_max","include/linux/overflow.h::__type_min","include/linux/overflow.h::type_min","include/linux/overflow.h::__overflows_type","include/linux/overflow.h::__overflows_type_constexpr","include/linux/overflow.h::overflows_type","include/linux/overflow.h::castable_to_type"],"text":"Checked arithmetic wraps compiler overflow builtins behind a must check boolean, wrapping forms return the wrapped result with optional in place assignment, type limit helpers derive extrema from width and signedness, and generic helpers test whether a value fits a destination type."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/overflow.h::check_shl_overflow","include/linux/overflow.h::__overflows_type_constexpr","include/linux/overflow.h::__overflows_type","include/linux/overflow.h::overflows_type","include/linux/overflow.h::range_overflows","include/linux/overflow.h::range_overflows_t","include/linux/overflow.h::range_end_overflows","include/linux/overflow.h::range_end_overflows_t","include/linux/overflow.h::castable_to_type"],"text":"Shift checking fails on negative or oversized shift amounts, negative inputs or outputs, and round trip mismatch, while range helpers require identically typed operands and distinguish start inclusive overflow from end exclusive overflow with optional pre cast variants."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/overflow.h::size_mul","include/linux/overflow.h::size_add","include/linux/overflow.h::size_sub","include/linux/overflow.h::array_size","include/linux/overflow.h::array3_size"],"text":"Size multiply, add and subtract return a maximum value sentinel on overflow, with subtract also saturating on sentinel inputs, and array helpers compose these primitives for two and three factor products."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/overflow.h::flex_array_size","include/linux/overflow.h::struct_size","include/linux/overflow.h::struct_size_t","include/linux/overflow.h::struct_offset","include/linux/overflow.h::__DEFINE_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::_DEFINE_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::DEFINE_RAW_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::DEFINE_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::STACK_FLEX_ARRAY_SIZE","include/linux/overflow.h::typeof_flex_counter","include/linux/overflow.h::overflows_flex_counter_type","include/linux/overflow.h::__set_flex_counter"],"text":"Flexible array sizing computes member times count plus whole struct totals with constant fast paths and saturating fallbacks, offset helper exposes member displacement, stack definition macros overlay a sized byte buffer with a typed pointer with optional initialization and counter setup, and counter helpers query capacity and assignment generically."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/overflow.h::flex_array_size","include/linux/overflow.h::struct_size","include/linux/overflow.h::struct_size_t","include/linux/overflow.h::__DEFINE_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::_DEFINE_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::DEFINE_RAW_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::DEFINE_FLEX","include/linux/overflow.h::STACK_FLEX_ARRAY_SIZE","include/linux/overflow.h::typeof_flex_counter","include/linux/overflow.h::overflows_flex_counter_type","include/linux/overflow.h::__set_flex_counter"],"text":"Flexible sizing requires a true trailing array member, stack forms demand a compile time count, constant counts use direct arithmetic while dynamic counts use saturating helpers, and counter access dispatches generically with a size type fallback when no counter exists."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/plist_types.h::plist_head","include/linux/plist_types.h::plist_node"],"text":"Priority list head holds a single node chain, while each node holds an integer priority plus separate chains for same priority linkage and global order linkage."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/plist.h::PLIST_HEAD_INIT","include/linux/plist.h::PLIST_HEAD","include/linux/plist.h::PLIST_NODE_INIT","include/linux/plist.h::plist_head_init","include/linux/plist.h::plist_node_init","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each_continue","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each_safe","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each_entry","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each_entry_continue","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each_entry_safe","include/linux/plist.h::plist_head_empty","include/linux/plist.h::plist_node_empty","include/linux/plist.h::plist_first","include/linux/plist.h::plist_last","include/linux/plist.h::plist_next","include/linux/plist.h::plist_prev","include/linux/plist.h::plist_first_entry.alt_1","include/linux/plist.h::plist_first_entry.alt_2","include/linux/plist.h::plist_last_entry.alt_1","include/linux/plist.h::plist_last_entry.alt_2"],"text":"Priority list interface provides static and runtime initialization for heads and nodes, iteration over the global chain with continue, safe against removal, and embedded entry variants, emptiness tests, ends access, neighbor stepping, and container conversion accessors."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/plist.h::plist_head_empty","include/linux/plist.h::plist_node_empty","include/linux/plist.h::plist_first","include/linux/plist.h::plist_last","include/linux/plist.h::plist_next","include/linux/plist.h::plist_prev","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each","include/linux/plist.h::plist_for_each_entry"],"text":"Global order follows the node chain sorted by priority, head emptiness derives from its chain, node emptiness derives from its own chain, first and last map to opposite chain ends, and neighbor steps move within the global chain."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/plist.h::plist_first_entry.alt_1","include/linux/plist.h::plist_first_entry.alt_2","include/linux/plist.h::plist_last_entry.alt_1","include/linux/plist.h::plist_last_entry.alt_2"],"text":"Ends accessors exist in two build variants, one warning when the head is empty before converting the node pointer and one converting unchecked, so callers must ensure non emptiness when using the unchecked form."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/radix-tree.h::radix_tree_preload"],"text":"Preload cache holds a local lock, a count of retained nodes, and a pointer to chained spare nodes linked through reuse of a parent field."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/radix-tree.h::radix_tree_root","include/linux/radix-tree.h::radix_tree_node"],"text":"Legacy radix names alias the extended array container and its node type for source compatibility."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_ENTRY_MASK","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_INTERNAL_NODE","include/linux/radix-tree.h::radix_tree_is_internal_node"],"text":"Entry tagging reserves the low two pointer bits as mask value three, with value two denoting an internal node, and a predicate reports internal status by masking and comparing."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_MAP_SHIFT","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_MAP_SIZE","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_MAP_MASK","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_MAX_TAGS","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_TAG_LONGS","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_INDEX_BITS","include/linux/radix-tree.h::RADIX_TREE_MAX_PATH"],"text":"Chunk shift derives from the extended array chunk size, map size is two raised to that shift with mask one less, tag capacity and longs derive from mark limits, index width equals unsigned long bits, and maximum depth is the rounded up division of width by shift."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/radix-tree.h::ROOT_IS_IDR"],"text":"Identifier radix root flag is a forced allocation flag value of four."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["include/linux/radix-tree.h::radix_tree_preload"],"text":"Preload structure carries a local lock guarding its spare node pool, with no acquisition order or critical section boundaries shown in these fragments."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/minmax.h::_LINUX_MINMAX_H","include/linux/overflow.h::__LINUX_OVERFLOW_H","include/linux/plist.h::_LINUX_PLIST_H_","include/linux/plist_types.h::_LINUX_PLIST_TYPES_H","include/linux/radix-tree.h::_LINUX_RADIX_TREE_H"],"text":"Each header defines a once only inclusion guard macro to prevent multiple inclusion."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ONCE.alt_1"],"text":"External once only warning helper owned elsewhere and relied upon by heap failure paths."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-